# Trivy's baseline for the image scan in .github/workflows/ci.yml (the
# `docker` job scans every image before it is pushed and fails on a
# fixable HIGH or CRITICAL). These are the advisories that were already
# open against the production dependencies when the gate went in — the
# same list pnpm-workspace.yaml's auditConfig.ignoreGhsas carries for
# `pnpm audit`, by the id Trivy reports (the CVE where one exists, the
# GHSA otherwise). Each line expires: past its date Trivy counts the
# finding again and the push fails, so fix the dependency and delete the
# line, or renew the date with a reason. Keep the two lists in step.

